senses.gloss:
pātayati (caus. of Skt. pat),
(1) puts back into a whole (what has been divided, to divide it again): ˚yitvā MSV 〔ii.119.19, and ff.〕;
(2) with roma (= Pali lomaṃ pāteti), lets (the hair) hang down, as sign of humble penitence (see romapāta and s.v. prakaca): Bhīk 〔28b.4〕; MSV 〔iii.7.14〕.

pātra, regularly nt.,
(1) with masc. forms, in Skt. mg. bowl: caturi pātrāṃ, acc. pl., LV 〔185.8〕 (vs); tenemi pātrāś (acc. pl.) caturaḥ … dadanti 〔385.7〕 (vs; in prec. line pātrāṇi);
(2) = Skt. yāna-pātra, ship (cf. Eng. vessel in same mg.; not recorded elsewhere), in siddha-pātra, with successful ship (after a voyage): Mv 〔iii.287.8〕; 〔288.15〕; 〔298.17〕; v.l. each time siddha-yānapātra, which is read in text with both mss. 〔iii.286.17〕.
